<p>A US federal judge in Massachusetts ruled that the Trump administration’s policy allowing rapid deportations of migrants to countries other than their own is unlawful, saying it violates due process protections. The decision targets so-called “third country” removals—sending people to a country they are not from—without what the judge considered adequate procedural safeguards. The judge stayed his ruling for 15 days to give the administration time to appeal.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/n73aQdFZOS8ncsaMlLMxk31mGGpm2EqSk3dk7Ot5n1fbdMpmSbD6gzq3I08potNFk4Z8wSXI7guqrgbMhspASXer7pik9QnnUiK7MntjzRuuG4UUh1C7HPr5IEvO16q3TfdGOJt-oPbVt6LKvhKJG8g1dTjZvMEUBuPHrWf06NBJ3ACZFxkC2_I' alt='Carlos Uzcategui, one of the Venezuelan migrants deported months ago to El Salvador by the United States under an immigration crackdown, is welcomed home in Lobatera, Venezuela, July 23, 2025.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>What the judge found: US District Judge Brian E. Murphy said the third-country removal process did not give migrants enough procedural protections before sending them to a country that is not their own, violating due process.</li><li>Destinations cited: Coverage of the policy said the administration has sent migrants to South Sudan and to El Salvador’s CECOT prison under this approach.</li><li>Supreme Court backdrop: Le Monde reported that a Supreme Court ruling last year strengthened the administration’s position; third-country transfers happened after that decision.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US District Judge Brian E. Murphy: He concluded the administration’s rapid third-country deportation process violates due process, which is why he blocked the policy. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-administrations-third-country-deportation-policy-is-unlawful-judge-rules/article70677160.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Trump administration: The judge’s 15-day pause gives the administration time to appeal, and it has signaled it plans to challenge the ruling. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-judge-rejects-trump-policy-allowing-swift-deportations-to-alternate-countries'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Migrants affected (as described): Reporting highlighted fears about transfers to places such as South Sudan or El Salvador’s CECOT prison, drawing attention to conditions in destination countries. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/02/25/trump-administration-s-third-country-deportation-policy-is-unlawful-judge-rules_6750874_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-judge-rejects-trump-policy-allowing-swift-deportations-to-alternate-countries'>Trump policy allowing swift deportations to alternate countries rejected by US judge</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/02/25/trump-administration-s-third-country-deportation-policy-is-unlawful-judge-rules_6750874_4.html'>Judge rules Trump administration&#x27;s &#x27;third country&#x27; deportation policy is unlawful</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-administrations-third-country-deportation-policy-is-unlawful-judge-rules/article70677160.ece'>Trump administration’s ’third country’ deportation policy is unlawful, judge rules</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/25/us-judge-rules-trump-policy-of-third-country-deportations-unlawful'>US judge rules Trump policy of ‘third country’ deportations unlawful</a> - aljazeera.com</li></ul>